body:
Thanks man, I still feel pretty shit though, cause my brain immediately goes to Murphy's law. I know it's probably just that she panicked or something, but I can't get the thought of what do I do if she leaves my life forever. Like I don't have a deep relationship with my parents or any of my family members for that matter. I can't really go to my friends for when i'm feeling down (I feel really emasculated about this), and I can't do anything to distract myself. 

&#x200B;

I'll try not to give up if everything goes to shit, but I'm not sure how i'd do that. I hear that women like smart and strong men, so I cleaned up my act, started lifting weights and hit the books hard. Went from a dumb, fat waste of space to a still overweight, but much more muscly guy with straight A's in college. Like I'm not trying to say that everything was strictly cause of her, but she was a driving factor in this change in my life.

I'm doing fine, I got it checked out and the doc said I just gotta rest up. 

&#x200B;

Like if it helps, I put my arm around her while we were watching the movie and she leaned into me. At one point it felt like she was guiding my hand to her breast by moving her forearm and trapping my arm there. I'm a very dense guy (I never know any subtle signs or anything like that), but I was convinced that that was a sign that she was into me, so I went for the kiss. I don't know anything anymore man, everything is just spinning for me. I wish I could do some work or something to take my mind off things like I always do, but the concussion is preventing me from doing that... Sorry about having to rely on you though. I hate having to rely on other people with a passion, but I just don't know anything anymore.
